{"availability":"available","full":"aniruddhaadak80/pqc-triage","name":"pqc-triage","description":"Import a real dependency manifest, see which cryptography a quantum computer breaks first, and commit the date you must migrate by.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-03T07:48:09Z","updated":"2026-10-04T10:52:24Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pqc-triage.vercel.app","topics":["cryptography","cybersecurity","developer-tools","harvest-now-decrypt-later","mcp","ml-kem","neon","nextjs","nist-ir-8547","opensource","post-quantum-cryptography","pqc-migration","quantum-computing","security","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://pqc-triage.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:21:32.668Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:21:32.668Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:21:32.668Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:46:24.891Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T18:21:32.668Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Find the cryptography a quantum computer breaks first — and the exact year you must migrate by.","[]( []( []( [](LICENSE) [](#data-provenance) [](#-agent-console) [](src/lib/engine.ts) [](#integrity-and-seal-replay)","Post-quantum migration is a calendar problem wearing a technical costume. Nobody argues about whether RSA-2048 falls to Shor's algorithm; everybody argues about when, and the honest answer is \"whatever year a cryptographically relevant quantum computer arrives\". Most inventories never get that far, because the first hard question is where the cryptography is."],"features":["Real inventory. Parses package-lock.json, package.json, requirements.txt,","go.mod, Gemfile.lock, composer.lock, Cargo.lock and pom.xml, then scans a source excerpt line by line for cryptographic call sites. Every surface carries the line it matched on.","A deadline, not a score. Mosca's rule: work must s